# --- Local development / tests (prisma/schema.prisma, SQLite) ---
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
AUTH_USER_EMAIL="daniel@example.com"
AUTH_SESSION_SECRET="change-me-in-production"
# Only read by prisma/seed.ts to hash the initial user's password; there is
# no AUTH_PASSWORD_HASH env var read anywhere at runtime (auth checks the
# User.passwordHash column via src/lib/auth.ts#verifyCredentials).
SEED_USER_PASSWORD=""

# --- Production only (Vercel project env vars, prisma/schema.production.prisma, PostgreSQL/Supabase) ---
# Same variable names as above, but set as Vercel Environment Variables —
# never written to a committed .env file. See "Deploy de produção" in
# README.md for exactly where to get each value and what NOT to share.
#   DATABASE_URL  — Supabase pooled connection string (pgbouncer, port 6543)
#   DIRECT_URL    — Supabase direct connection string (port 5432), used only
#                   by `prisma migrate deploy` for DDL
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY  — same key, or omit to run on the rule-based parser only
#   AUTH_USER_EMAIL    — Daniel's real login email
#   AUTH_SESSION_SECRET — a new, strong, production-only secret (never reuse
#                          the dev one)
